VK: drop the stages of shader features the device lacks from stage masks.

GetPipelineStageFlags and GetShaderStageFlags (ConversionVK.h) turn a mask naming every shader
stage ("StageBits::ALL_SHADERS" in a barrier or a fence wait, a pipeline layout whose stages are
"ALL") into every Vulkan stage bit, whatever the device has. On a device without tessellation,
geometry, task, mesh or ray tracing shaders the validation layer then refuses the barrier
(VUID-VkMemoryBarrier2-srcStageMask-07946 / -dstStageMask-07946 for the ray tracing stage, 03929,
03934 and 03935 for geometry, mesh and task), the push constant range and the push
(VUID-VkPushConstantRange-stageFlags-parameter, VUID-VkPushConstantsInfo-stageFlags-parameter: ray
tracing, task and mesh shader stage bits without their extension). Measured on v191: MoltenVK
(no geometry, mesh or ray tracing) and NVIDIA with "disableVKRayTracing". CmdSetDescriptorSet
already adds the mesh stages only with "features.meshShader".

DeviceVK records the shader stages it lacks once, from the features it enabled; barriers and
fence waits drop their pipeline stages, and a pipeline layout drops them from its stages, which
"ALL" and "ALL_SHADERS" resolve to.

